      "full_text": "Strahilevitz is standing by February 03, 2013 12:15 PM Eastern Standard Time SAN FRANCISCO--(BUSINESS WIRE)--Professor of Marketing, Michal Ann Strahilevitz of Golden Gate University in San Francisco has been teaching Advertising Strategy to MBA students for more than a decade. She has also been commenting on the Super Bowl ad phenomenon for years \u2014 especially how in recent years, social media has changed the game. If you\u2019d like her 2013 insights (as well as this 2/1 article), contact Robb Shephard at rkfghj@kkonlh.qnzzc.com. Here\u2019s Dr. Strahilevitz's bio: http://www.ggu.edu/faculty/michal-strahldevitz. But first, if you want her thoughts today (Saturday) \u2014 and certainly not tomorrow! \u2014 she is game to talk! So here are some quick questions to get things started: 1a - What will you be doing Super Bowl Sunday? 2. How many times have you seen each year's lineup of commercials? 3. Favorite category? Why? Least favorite: why",
